# AI Agent Rules — React + TypeScript + shadcn/ui Project

## 1. Purpose

This file defines architectural rules, naming conventions, and coding patterns for AI coding agents working in a React + TypeScript project. Follow these rules precisely when reading, writing, or refactoring code.

**UI library: this project uses [shadcn/ui](https://ui.shadcn.com) (Radix primitives + Tailwind + `class-variance-authority`), configured via `app/components.json`.** It does **not** use HeroUI, MUI, Chakra, Ant Design, or any other component library. Before adding any UI dependency or writing a new primitive:

1. Check `app/src/components/ui/` for an existing shadcn component first (run `ls app/src/components/ui`).
2. If the primitive doesn't exist yet, generate it with the shadcn CLI (`npx shadcn@latest add <component>` from `app/`) so it lands in `components/ui/` with the project's existing style (`new-york`, `neutral` base color, `cssVariables: true` — see `components.json`), instead of hand-rolling a custom component or pulling in a different UI library.
3. Never import from `@heroui/react`, `@mui/*`, `@chakra-ui/*`, `antd`, or similar — they are not installed and must not be added without an explicit user request.
4. All shadcn primitives are Radix-based: `open`/`onOpenChange` for overlays (`Dialog`, `Sheet`, `Popover`, `AlertDialog`), `disabled` for disabled state — not React Aria APIs like `useOverlayState` or `isDismissable` (those belong to HeroUI/React Aria, not this stack).

