## 2. Project Structure Guidelines

```
src/
├── App.tsx                        # Root: Router > QueryProvider > AppRoutes
├── main.tsx                       # Entry point
├── index.css                      # Tailwind v4 CSS-first config + CSS variables
├── DESIGN.md                      # Design system (Material Design 3) — read before UI work
├── routes/
│   └── routes.ts                  # Centralized Routes object (all frontend paths)
├── config/
│   ├── api/
│   │   ├── axios.ts               # Axios instance with auth interceptor
│   │   └── routes.ts              # Centralized ApiRoutes object (all API endpoints)
│   ├── environments/
│   │   └── index.ts               # Typed and exported env vars
│   └── constants/                 # Static maps and dropdown options
│       └── dropdowns/             # Select/ListBox option arrays by domain folder
├── features/                      # Domain modules (see Feature Module Pattern)
├── pages/                         # Route-level page components
├── components/
│   ├── layout/                    # Layout shells (sidebar, header, etc.)
│   ├── ui/                        # shadcn/ui base components + custom primitives
│   └── providers/                 # React context providers
├── stores/                        # Zustand stores
├── hooks/                         # Global reusable hooks (not feature-specific)
├── lib/                           # Pure utility functions (incl. dropdown-option-label.utils.ts)
├── interfaces/                    # Shared cross-domain interfaces
└── types/                         # Global TypeScript declarations
```

### Feature Module Pattern

Every domain feature lives in `src/features/<feature-name>/` and follows this structure:

```
features/<feature-name>/
├── hooks/
│   └── use-<feature-name>.ts         # TanStack Query hooks (useQuery / useMutation)
├── interfaces/
│   └── <feature-name>.interfaces.ts  # TypeScript interfaces + DTO types + const enums
├── services/
│   └── <feature-name>.services.ts    # Plain async functions wrapping axiosInstance
└── validation-schemas/               # (optional — only if feature has forms)
    └── <feature-name>.schema.ts      # Zod schemas + inferred types
```

Optional `utils/` under a feature is only for **non-UI business helpers** (e.g. payload mappers, link resolution from API shapes). It must **not** contain enum labels, select options, descriptions, or other static display vocabulary — those belong in `config/constants/dropdowns/`.

**Never create `components/` under `features/`.** Features are data-only modules (hooks, services, interfaces, schemas). All React UI lives in `pages/<section>/components/` or `components/ui/`.

### Page Structure

Pages live in `src/pages/<section>/` and may contain nested sub-pages:

```
pages/<section>/
├── index.tsx                      # Top-level page component (route entry)
├── components/                    # Page-local components (not reused elsewhere)
├── hooks/                         # Page-local hooks (UI state only, no API calls)
├── pages/                         # Sub-pages (e.g., new-item, edit-item)
├── utils/                         # Page-local utility functions
└── validation-schemas/            # Page-local Zod schemas (if not in features/)
```

**Do:** Put all data-fetching logic in `features/`. Pages import hooks, services, interfaces, and schemas from features.  
**Don't:** Put API calls, Zod schemas, or React components inside `features/`.  
**Don't:** Create `features/<feature-name>/components/` — page-local UI belongs in `pages/<section>/components/`.

### Static UI vocabulary (dropdowns, labels, descriptions)

**All static human-readable enum vocabulary belongs in `src/config/constants/dropdowns/`.** This is not limited to `<Select>` / `<ListBox>` data. It includes anything that maps a domain enum/id to display text:

- Filter/toolbar select options (`{ id, label }[]`)
- Form select options (`{ id, label }[]`)
- Short descriptions shown in cards or help text (`{ id, description }[]` or `Record<Enum, string>`)
- Chip/badge/table display labels for enum values
- `get<Entity><Field>Label()` / `get<Entity><Field>Description()` helpers tied to that vocabulary

**Canonical location:** `src/config/constants/dropdowns/<domain-folder>/<domain>-<context>.options.ts`

Domain folders: `agencies`, `scrapers`, `properties`, `integrations`, `notifications`, `users`, `jobs`, `shared`.

**Never put this data in:**

- `features/**/utils/**` (including `*-label.utils.ts`, `*-description.utils.ts`, `*-options.ts`)
- `pages/**/components/**` or `pages/**/index.tsx` (no inline `const xLabel: Record<...>` / `const xOptions = [...]`)
- `pages/**/utils/**`
- `features/**/components/**`
- `lib/**` (except the single shared reader below)

`features/` is **data-only** (hooks, services, interfaces, validation-schemas). It must not own display labels, select options, or React UI.

#### File naming

One file per option set, under the matching domain folder. Use a suffix that matches usage:

| Suffix | Purpose | Example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `-filter.options.ts` | Toolbar/filter `<Select>` with `{ id: T \| "all", label }` | `agencies/agency-status-filter.options.ts` |
| `-form.options.ts` | Form `<Select>` with `{ id: T, label }` — often the **canonical label source** | `integrations/integration-type-form.options.ts` |
| `-description.options.ts` | Card/help copy keyed by enum | `integrations/integration-type-description.options.ts` |
| `.options.ts` (no suffix) | Shared static lists not tied to filter/form | `shared/country.options.ts`, `shared/timezone.options.ts` |

**Export naming:** `PascalCase` + `Options` suffix (`AgencyStatusFilterOptions`, `IntegrationTypeFormOptions`).

#### Shapes

- **Filter:** `{ id: T | "all"; label: string }[]` — first entry `{ id: "all", label: "..." }` when applicable
- **Form:** `{ id: T; label: string }[]`
- **Description:** `{ id: T; description: string }[]` or `Record<T, string>` when labels are not `{ id, label }[]`
- Import enum types from `@/features/<feature>/interfaces/` — dropdown files do not redefine enums

#### Canonical source & reuse (mandatory)

When the same enum labels appear in filter + form + chips + tables:

1. Define labels once in `<domain>-form.options.ts` (or the filter file if there is no form select).
2. `<domain>-filter.options.ts` spreads the form/canonical list: `[{ id: "all", ... }, ...FormOptions]`.
3. `<domain>-description.options.ts` holds descriptions only — do not duplicate labels there.
4. **Do not** import dropdown data from `features/**`. Dropdown files may import types from `features/**/interfaces/` only.

#### Label/description getters

- Export `get<Domain><Context>Label()` / `get<Domain><Context>Description()` from the **same** `*.options.ts` file that owns the data.
- For reading labels from a filter/form options array in chips or tables, use the shared helper  
  `getDropdownOptionLabel()` from `@/lib/dropdown-option-label.utils.ts` — do **not** copy a local `find()` helper per component.
- Do **not** create per-domain label utils under `features/` or `pages/`.

#### Chips, badges, and tables

Status/type chips **must** resolve display text from `config/constants/dropdowns/` (via `getDropdownOptionLabel` or a co-located `get*Label`).

**Wrong — label map in a chip component:**

```tsx
const statusLabel: Record<AgencyStatus, string> = {
  [AgencyStatuses.ACTIVE]: "Active",
  ...
};
<Chip.Label>{statusLabel[status]}</Chip.Label>
```

**Correct:**

```tsx
import { AgencyStatusFilterOptions } from "@/config/constants/dropdowns/agencies/agency-status-filter.options";
import { getDropdownOptionLabel } from "@/lib/dropdown-option-label.utils";

<Chip.Label>{getDropdownOptionLabel(AgencyStatusFilterOptions, status)}</Chip.Label>
```

Chip color maps (`Record<Enum, ChipColor>`) may stay in the chip component — only **text vocabulary** is centralized.

#### Hard bans (agents must not generate)

- `features/<feature>/utils/*-label.utils.ts`
- `features/<feature>/utils/*-description.utils.ts`
- `features/<feature>/utils/*-options.ts`
- `const <name>Options = [...]` or `const <name>Label: Record<...>` in pages/components (except the exceptions below)
- `features/<feature>/components/**` for any UI, including chips and forms
- Dropdown files that re-export data from `features/**/utils/**`
- Duplicating the same `{ id, label }` list in a second file when an existing `*.options.ts` already defines it
- Using `enumValue.replace(/_/g, " ")` or `role.replace("_", " ")` for user-visible labels when a dropdown options file exists or should exist

#### Allowed exceptions

- **Runtime/API-derived options only** — mapping fetched entities to `{ id, label }` in the component or hook that owns that query (e.g. connection picker built from `useUserIntegrationConnections()`).
- **Ephemeral action menus** — row action definitions local to a table (`{ id: "delete", label: "Delete" }`) when they are not reused enum vocabulary.
- **Chip color maps** — visual styling keyed by enum, not display strings.

#### Agent checklist (before finishing any UI task)

1. Adding or changing enum display text? → edit/create `config/constants/dropdowns/<domain>/*.options.ts` first.
2. Need a label in a chip, table cell, modal title, or card? → import from dropdowns; never add a local `Record<..., string>`.
3. Filter and form share labels? → one canonical file; filter spreads it.
4. Tempted to add `features/.../utils/...label...`? → stop; use dropdowns.
5. New enum value? → update **every** related `*.options.ts` (form, filter, description, chips) in the same change.

