## 3. Naming Conventions

### Files

- All files: `kebab-case` (e.g., `use-feature-name.ts`, `feature-name.services.ts`)
- Exception: shadcn/ui components may use `PascalCase.tsx`

### Components

- Function names: `PascalCase`
- Page components: `<Domain>Page`
- Modal components: `<Domain>Modal`
- Form components: `<Domain>Form`

### Hooks

- File: `use-kebab-case.ts`
- Function: `useCamelCase` (e.g., file `use-feature-name.ts` → exports `useFeatureName`)
- Query hooks: `useGet<Entity>` or `use<Entity>`
- Mutation hooks: `useCreate<Entity>`, `useUpdate<Entity>`, `useDelete<Entity>`

### Types and Interfaces

- Interface files: `<feature>.interfaces.ts`
- Interface names: `PascalCase`, no `I` prefix
- DTO types: `<Action><Entity>Dto` (e.g., `CreateEntityDto`, `UpdateEntityDto`)
- Query param types: `<Entity>QueryType` or `<Entity>Query`

### Validation Schemas

- File: `<feature>.schema.ts`
- Schema names: `camelCase` + `Schema` suffix (e.g., `createEntitySchema`)
- Inferred types: `<Action><Entity>FormData` or `<Entity>FormValues`

### Zustand Stores

- File: `<domain>.ts` in `src/stores/`
- Hook export: `use<Domain>Store`
- State accessor: `get<Domain>StoreState()` (for non-React contexts)
- Store key constant: `const STORE_KEY = "<domain>"` (kebab-case string)

---

## 4. Component Guidelines

- Page components manage modal open/close state and selected entity identifier
- Delegate API calls to feature hooks; delegate UI state to page-local hooks
- Use `FC` type annotation with explicit props interface
- Default export for pages and layouts; named exports for reusable components
- shadcn/ui components live in `components/ui/` and must not be modified directly — extend via wrappers
- Use `variant` prop pattern from `class-variance-authority` (cva) in base UI components

### Shared UI reuse (`components/ui/`)

**Before creating any new UI primitive**, list and read what already exists under `app/src/components/ui/`. Reuse or extend an existing component instead of duplicating markup in a page. Visual tokens and patterns live in `app/DESIGN.md`.

Current shared primitives (non-exhaustive — extend this list as new ones land, and always check the real directory first):

| File | Use for |
| --- | --- |
| `button.tsx` | All buttons. Use the built-in `loading` prop (`<Button loading={mutation.isPending}>`) for submit/destructive actions while a mutation is pending — it shows a spinner and disables itself. Do not build a separate "button with pending" wrapper. |
| `dialog.tsx` | Modals/dialogs (shadcn `Dialog`, Radix-based) |
| `confirmation-dialog.tsx` | Destructive confirmations (delete, disconnect) — a `Dialog` wrapper with `isOpen` / `onClose` / `onConfirm` props |
| `select.tsx`, `select-dropdown.tsx` | Selects (shadcn `Select`, Radix-based) |
| `table.tsx` | Data tables (shadcn `Table`) |
| `skeleton.tsx` | Loading placeholders (shadcn `Skeleton`) |
| `password-input.tsx`, `phone-input.tsx`, `pin-input.tsx` | Specialized credential/contact form inputs |
| `form.tsx` | React Hook Form field wrappers (shadcn `Form`) |
| `toast.tsx` / `toaster.tsx` | Mutation feedback (paired with the `toast()` helper in `@/hooks/use-toast`) |
| `pagination.tsx` | List/table pagination controls |
| `sidebar.tsx` | App navigation shell |

**Placement rule:**

- **Used by one page route** → `pages/<section>/components/` (import via `./components/<file>`)
- **Used by multiple pages in the same section** (e.g. admin list + detail) → `pages/<section>/components/` (shared within that section folder)
- **Used by multiple pages across sections** → copy into each page's `components/` folder **or** promote to `app/src/components/ui/` when the component is presentational and identical everywhere
- **Reused app-wide primitives** (buttons, skeletons, dialogs) → `app/src/components/ui/`

**Never** place UI in `features/<feature>/components/`. If a form or chip is tied to a domain, colocate it with the page that renders it and import domain types/hooks from `@/features/<feature>/`.

When adding a shared component to `components/ui/`, keep it presentational — no API calls, no feature hooks.

### Loading states — shadcn `Skeleton` only

While TanStack Query reports `isPending` / `isLoading`, render a **layout-shaped skeleton** — never a text label.

**Do not use:** `"Loading..."`, `"Please wait"`, centered spinner-only placeholders, or any loading copy as the primary loading UI.

**Do use:** `Skeleton` from `@/components/ui/skeleton`, sized to match the final layout (table rows, detail header, form fields, card grid):

```tsx
import { Skeleton } from "@/components/ui/skeleton";

if (isPending) {
  return (
    <div className="flex flex-col gap-3">
      {Array.from({ length: 8 }).map((_, i) => (
        <Skeleton key={i} className="h-10 w-full rounded-lg" />
      ))}
    </div>
  );
}
```

When the same skeleton layout appears on more than one page, extract it to `app/src/components/ui/` **after checking no equivalent already exists**.

For the triggering control on a mutation, use `Button`'s built-in `loading` prop (`<Button loading={mutation.isPending}>Save</Button>`) — that is not a page-level loading label, so it's fine even while a full-page skeleton isn't warranted.

### Destructive actions — `ConfirmationDialog`

**Never** delete or disconnect on a bare button press. Always confirm through the shared `ConfirmationDialog` in `components/ui/confirmation-dialog.tsx` (a shadcn `Dialog` wrapper).

Pattern:

```tsx
import { useState } from "react";
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";
import ConfirmationDialog from "@/components/ui/confirmation-dialog";

const [isDeleteOpen, setIsDeleteOpen] = useState(false);

<Button variant="destructive" onClick={() => setIsDeleteOpen(true)}>Delete</Button>

<ConfirmationDialog
  isOpen={isDeleteOpen}
  onClose={() => setIsDeleteOpen(false)}
  onConfirm={() => deleteTarget.mutateAsync(id)}
  title="Delete integration target?"
  description="This action cannot be undone."
  confirmText="Delete"
  variant="destructive"
  isLoading={deleteTarget.isPending}
/>
```

Use `confirmText="Disconnect"` for user integration disconnect flows. Reuse the same component — do not build one-off alert modals per page.

### shadcn `Dialog` (modals)

Modals use the shadcn `Dialog` (Radix-based) from `components/ui/dialog.tsx`. State is a plain boolean (`useState`, or lifted to the page as in the Page Component example below) passed as `open` and toggled via `onOpenChange` — there is no separate overlay-state hook to import.

```tsx
import { useState } from "react";
import { Dialog, DialogContent, DialogHeader, DialogTitle, DialogFooter } from "@/components/ui/dialog";
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";

const [isOpen, setIsOpen] = useState(false);

<Dialog open={isOpen} onOpenChange={setIsOpen}>
  <DialogContent>
    <DialogHeader>
      <DialogTitle>Edit agency</DialogTitle>
    </DialogHeader>
    {/* form content */}
    <DialogFooter>
      <Button variant="outline" onClick={() => setIsOpen(false)}>Cancel</Button>
      <Button loading={mutation.isPending} onClick={handleSubmit}>Save</Button>
    </DialogFooter>
  </DialogContent>
</Dialog>
```

Guard closing while a mutation is in flight by ignoring `onOpenChange(false)` (or disabling the trigger) when `mutation.isPending` is true, instead of looking for an `isDismissable` prop — shadcn's `Dialog` doesn't have one.

### shadcn `Table`

Compose `Table` with `TableHeader` / `TableBody` directly — there is no separate scroll-container or collection wrapper to nest through.

```tsx
import { Table, TableHeader, TableBody, TableRow, TableHead, TableCell } from "@/components/ui/table";

<Table>
  <TableHeader>
    <TableRow>
      <TableHead>Name</TableHead>
      <TableHead>Email</TableHead>
    </TableRow>
  </TableHeader>
  <TableBody>
    {rows.map((row) => (
      <TableRow key={row.id}>
        <TableCell>{row.name}</TableCell>
        <TableCell>{row.email}</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
    ))}
  </TableBody>
</Table>
```

### shadcn `Select`

Every `Select` needs an accessible name: a visible `<Label htmlFor>` for form fields, or `aria-label` on the trigger for toolbar/filter selects without a visible label.

**Form fields — pair with a `<Label>` (or use inside shadcn `Form`/`FormField`, which wires this up automatically):**

```tsx
import { Label } from "@/components/ui/label";
import { Select, SelectTrigger, SelectValue, SelectContent, SelectItem } from "@/components/ui/select";

<div className="space-y-2">
  <Label htmlFor="agency">Agency</Label>
  <Select value={value} onValueChange={setValue}>
    <SelectTrigger id="agency">
      <SelectValue placeholder="Select an agency" />
    </SelectTrigger>
    <SelectContent>
      <SelectItem value="active">Active</SelectItem>
    </SelectContent>
  </Select>
</div>
```

**Toolbar / filter selects without visible labels — use `aria-label` on the trigger:**

```tsx
<Select value={status} onValueChange={setStatus}>
  <SelectTrigger aria-label="Filter by status">
    <SelectValue />
  </SelectTrigger>
  <SelectContent>...</SelectContent>
</Select>
```

